## ROLLBACK (W3; only on a Step 5/6 failure; once; as Stamp S7 allows)
**Single revision mode** (MEASURED: `activeRevisionsMode` `Single`): the guide's rollback is to deploy the recorded image again, which makes a new revision running it (guide lines 237 to 251). Verbatim:
`AZURE_CONFIG_DIR='<P>/4_Credentials/.azure' az containerapp update -n nexusaidev-app -g nexusai-dev-rg --container-name nexusai-api --image nexusaidevacrfa39.azurecr.io/nexusai@sha256:c12c43e538f1274c1a7ba180f2cdfd595be63ec16eee0e45c690903734e08e4f --query properties.latestRevisionName -o tsv`
Then the whole of Step 6 against the anchor: sole active = the rollback revision with the anchor digest (Step 6.1 poll), health OK with build `def3ac7e654fdacd` (6.3), env pairs equal to `ev/env-before.tsv` (6.4), the boot lines (6.5). No env was changed by the swap, so no `--set-env-vars` or `--remove-env-vars` belongs in the rollback. Final line `ROLLED BACK B1991: <reason>; live <revision> build def3ac7e654fdacd`. The product owner is told through Tuesday (routing row C6 says any rollback is told to the product owner; that is Tuesday's to send, not yours).
**Why not "re-activate the previous revision and move traffic back":** read by `--help` only (`az containerapp revision activate --revision`, `az containerapp ingress traffic set --revision-weight`): in Single mode the ingress sends 100% to the latest revision, so an activated old revision takes no traffic without first switching the app to `Multiple` mode, which is a setting change this kit does not allow. Neither command is run in this kit.
If the rollback itself fails any check: STOP at once, write everything measured, last line `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY rollback failed: <check>; demo serves <revision/build>`. Never a second rollback, never a third image.

